    "title": "Qualify adaptive sparse M3TQ lookup with the existing recipe engine",
    "url": "https://github.com/hsoliwal/com.synexia/pull/9726",
    "body": "A one-key warm containment query currently scans 32,766 prepared source keys. This packet uses the existing hash-pinned Java engine to produce an adaptive sparse lookup candidate, retaining the dense merge and exact set-inclusion semantics.\n\nValidation: 3 OpenRewrite SDK execution/fixed-point/refusal tests pass. Exact uninstrumented kernels pass 31,011 new and 308,649 existing JNI-backed checks in mixed, interpreter, C1 and C2 modes. The deterministic instrumented work probe falls from 32,766 source-key reads to 16. Three-fork host-kernel smoke timings, controls and raw evidence are included; early-hit overhead is disclosed.\n\nCanonical tooling/templates stay in Synexia; M3jdk21 receives generated source/test and a thin receipt. Full custom JVM image/jtreg, end-to-end String/JMH, retained-memory and older receiving-snapshot reconciliation remain pending. Keep this draft paired with the target candidate until receiving gates are resolved. Existing develop history and canonical engine are preserved.\n\nPaired receiving candidate: [M3jdk21 #366](https://github.com/hsoliwal/M3jdk21/pull/366). The unchanged baseline and candidate share the pre-existing `HOLD_MATCHER_STATE_GAP` admission failure; target receipts retain both outputs."
  },
